.TH SMARTPNGDIFF 1 "2026-09-03" "smartmet-library-regression" "SmartMet Regression Tools"
.SH NAME
smartpngdiff \- compare a PNG against a reference and report PSNR pass/fail
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B smartpngdiff
.I ok_png
.I png
.I diff_png
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B smartpngdiff
is the visual\(hyregression test driver used by SmartMet test suites.
It compares a freshly produced PNG against a reference PNG, writes a
difference image, and classifies the result by peak signal\(hyto\(hynoise
ratio.
.PP
Both helper programs are searched for next to
.B smartpngdiff
itself first and then on the
.BR PATH .
.SS PSNR verdict
The PSNR is measured by
.BR smartimagediff_psnr (1)
and is authoritative: it alone decides the reported verdict and the
exit status.
.RS 4
.IP \(bu 2
.B PSNR == infinity
\(em images are bit\(hyidentical;
.B OK
is reported and the script exits with status
.BR 0 .
.IP \(bu 2
.B PSNR >= 50 dB
\(em differences below visual threshold;
.B OK
with the PSNR value, exit
.BR 0 .
.IP \(bu 2
.B "20 dB <= PSNR < 50 dB"
\(em
.B WARNING
with the PSNR value, exit
.BR 0 .
.IP \(bu 2
.B PSNR < 20 dB
\(em
.B FAIL
with the PSNR value, exit
.BR 100 .
.IP \(bu 2
PSNR could not be parsed (corrupt image, dimension mismatch, etc.)
\(em
.BR FAIL ,
exit
.BR 100 .
.RE
.PP
If the
.I png
input does not exist the script prints
.B "*** FAILED: '...' not created"
and exits with status
.BR 255 .
.SS Structural comparison (shadow mode)
When
.BR smartimagediff (1)
is available it is run as well. It writes
.IR diff_png ,
which shows one image faded to faint grayscale with the clustered
changes painted red and boxed, so the eye lands on a real regression
instead of the equalized full\(hyframe edge noise. Its verdict does not
affect the exit status; it is appended to every verdict line as
.PP
.RS 4
.BI [sid: label " " info ]
.RE
.PP
where
.I label
is
.BR OK ,
.BR FAIL ,
.B ERROR
(the program failed to run) or
.B SKIP
(the program was not found), and
.I info
is its first output line (cluster and changed\(hypixel counts). When the
structural and the PSNR verdicts reach opposite pass/fail conclusions,
the line is prefixed with
.BR SHADOW-DISAGREE ,
which is the greppable signal for comparing the two comparators on a
real test run. Thresholds of the structural comparison can be tuned
with its
.B SID_*
environment variables.
.PP
Without
.BR smartimagediff (1)
the difference image is produced the legacy way instead, by piping the
two inputs through
.BR composite (1)
with the
.B \-compose DIFFERENCE
operator and through
.B convert
(or
.BR magick (1))
with
.B "\-contrast-stretch 0"
so that even small per\(hypixel deviations become visible.
.PP
ANSI colour output is suppressed when the
.B CI
environment variable is set, so test logs in CI remain plain text.
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I ok_png
Reference PNG (the expected image).
.TP
.I png
Actual PNG produced by the test under inspection.
.TP
.I diff_png
Path to write the difference image.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
PSNR in the OK or WARNING range, or images identical.
.TP
.B 100
PSNR below threshold or comparison failed.
.TP
.B 255
Actual PNG file is missing.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
.RS 4
smartpngdiff results_ok/contour.png results/contour.png \\
.br
.RS 0
.RE
.RS 4
results_diff/contour.png
.RE
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR smartimagediff_psnr (1),
.BR smartimagediff (1),
.BR composite (1),
.BR convert (1),
.BR magick (1)
.SH AUTHOR
Finnish Meteorological Institute
.PP
Report issues at <https://github.com/fmidev/smartmet-library-regression/issues>.
